# Blank lines inside fn bodies

Applies to every Rust fn you write or edit, any length, tests included.
Blank lines are free: `code_lines` (`crates/rstyle-core/src/lines.rs`) doesn't count them.

- Separate logical phases with one blank line: setup/bindings, the main work, the result.
- A comment line directly above a phase counts as its header; the blank goes above the comment.
- Never more than one blank in a row. No blank right after `{` or right before `}`.
- A body that is a single phase (one expression, one chain) needs none.
- When editing an existing fn, fix its spacing too if you touch more than a line.

```rust
// ❌ BAD
fn fn_length(f: &FnFacts, cfg: &Config) -> Vec<Diagnostic> {
    let actual = code_lines(&f.source);
    let limit = cfg.fn_length.max_lines;
    let message = format!("function `{}` is too long", f.name);
    (actual > limit)
        .then(|| diagnostic(f, "fn_length", message, Measure { actual, limit }))
        .into_iter()
        .collect()
}

// ✅ GOOD
fn fn_length(f: &FnFacts, cfg: &Config) -> Vec<Diagnostic> {
    let actual = code_lines(&f.source);
    let limit = cfg.fn_length.max_lines;
    let message = format!("function `{}` is too long", f.name);

    (actual > limit)
        .then(|| diagnostic(f, "fn_length", message, Measure { actual, limit }))
        .into_iter()
        .collect()
}
```
